<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bayezid I</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sultan Bayezid I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bayezid I was an Ottoman sultan of the late fourteenth century, known for rapid conquests in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. He was defeated and captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ankara">Battle of Ankara</a> in 1402. The defeat temporarily destroyed Ottoman military power and triggered a long succession crisis, an episode central to the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bayezid-i.jpg" alt="Bayezid I" width="314" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1460 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_accession_of_Sultan_Bayezid_I_(enthroned)._Ahmed%C3%AE,_Iskendername,_VBNM,_circa_1460.,_Cod._Or._XC_(57),_y._240b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
